Committed as `6a50dff`. 

## Summary

**Improvement:** `truncate_at_word_boundary` (src/format/mod.rs) silently blew its `max_bytes` budget — it appended the 3-byte `"…"` suffix on top of a `max_bytes`-sized truncation, returning up to `max_bytes + 3` bytes. This was inconsistent with its documented sibling `safe_truncate_with_suffix`, which explicitly counts the suffix toward the budget (and has a test asserting `len() == 8`).

**The fix:** reserve bytes for the ellipsis before truncating (`budget = max_bytes - "…".len()`), so the total never exceeds `max_bytes`. Used by topic-preview paths in `prompt_utils.rs` and `commands_session.rs` (both pass `50`).

**Tests first (4 new, all failed before the fix):**
• `"hello world"` @ 10 → was 13 bytes (`"hello worl…"`), now ≤ 10
• `"the quick brown fox jumps"` @ 20 → was 22 bytes, now exactly `"the quick brown…"` (18 bytes, word boundary kept)
• multibyte `✓` case → was 15 bytes, now ≤ 12, no panic
• short-string unchanged / empty-string cases

**Verification:** `cargo fmt` + `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` + `cargo build` + `cargo test` all pass (4310 bin + 88 integration tests). No docs affected — internal helper behavior only. Committed immediately after green.
